<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20176" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hālo</span></b> , āvi, ātum,
		1, v. n. and <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a.</i>, <i>to breathe</i> (<b>poet.</b>; cf.: feo, spiro). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Neutr.</i>, <i>to breathe</i>, <i>to emit vapor</i> or <i>fragrance</i>, <i>be fragrant</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">invitent croceis halantes floribus horti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 4, 109</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ture calent arae sertisque recentibus halant,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. A.
					1, 417</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>to breathe out</i>, <i>exhale</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">et nardi florem, nectar qui naribus halat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					2, 848</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">6, 221</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">391</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 10,
			48</span></i>. </div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
